  "entity_raw": {
    "name_raw": "Improved Infuse Weapon",
    "definition_type_raw": null,
    "source_book_raw": "Demons Revisited pg. 38",
    "definition_raw": "Source Demons Revisited pg. 38\nWhen you infuse weapons, you may add an additional magical quality.\n\nPrerequisites: Infuse weapon special ability, Cha 27\n\nBenefit: When you infuse a weapon, you can add an additional +1 worth of weapon qualities to that weapon; this could either be used to increase a weapon infused to be a +1 weapon to be a +2 weapon, or to grant a weapon quality like flaming, defending, keen, or any other +1 quality from the Pathfinder RPG Core Rulebook. This effect occurs automatically as you infuse a weapon, but you may only do so to one weapon you wield at a time.\n\nSpecial: You may take this feat more than once; each time you do, the limit to the number of weapons on which you can simultaneously use Improved Infuse Weapon increases by 2.",
    "links_raw": [
      {
        "anchor_text_raw": "Demons Revisited pg. 38",
